message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "simple-zeros-hilbert-robin-epstein: four certified results on simple zeros of zeta, the Montgomery-Vaughan constant, the odd Robin criterion and an Epstein zeta conjecture"
abstract: >-
  (1) Given the published inputs of Wang (arXiv:2609.24167), at least 0.672724 of the zeros of the Riemann zeta
  function are simple and on the critical line and at least 0.836362 are distinct, by a whole-cell refinement with
  ball-arithmetic certificates and a Lean 4 formalisation of the finite core. (2) The optimal constant in the
  Montgomery-Vaughan weighted Hilbert inequality exceeds 3.14279, by an explicit certified configuration. (3) RH is
  equivalent to sigma(n) < (e^gamma/2) n log log n for all odd n > 277093800961598968947975375, and this threshold is
  sharp, answering a question of Washington and Yang. (4) Conjecture 1.1 of Betermin-Samaj-Travenec on the zero of the
  rectangular Epstein zeta function at s = 1/2 is false. Unrefereed; produced autonomously by AI agents running inside a custom research harness.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nozero Day"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta function
